I don't have the dumpfile for the game, since I started another one soon 
after. But I can give you some of the amusing tales of the ascension.

I wished for 3 AoLS to go for the tourney record. I had also planned to 
either find more or polypile a bunch of amulets to try and get one. A 
wand never materialized. Nor did a scroll of genocide - because I wished 
for amulets (and a =oLev, SDSM, scrolls of charging and a blessed magic 
marker) I had to contend with the liches and mind flayers along the way 
(which caused me to forget some of the levels I had crossed and what 
some items in my inventory were).

Before the ascension run I found a blessed magic lamp. Great! I made one 
last run to the main dungeon, sacked some things, converted potions to 
holy water, and rubbed the lamp. I got a stupid genie with no wish.

By now, my patience was at an end. I was unable to find a WoPolymorph to 
try and get an AoLS by polypiling an amulet collection I had amassed. So 
I killed the genie. At which point I heard rumbling in the distance. How 
nice - in my anger I forgot he was generated as a pet. Screw it, I 
thought, I'll ascend regardless.

So I took the book from Rodney, killed the high priest with a WoD and 
made a mad dash for the exit. I don't know if it was the new moon, or me 
killing the genie, or what - but I had to kill Rodney not once, not 
twice, not 8 times like Zeitgeist - I had to kill him *19 times.* He 
appeared on every single plane (except astral) and double troubled at 
least four times.

I used all the AoLS by the time I got to the Astral. However, conflict 
and a c corpse helped pave the way. I found the high altar on my second 
attempt.

Later on I checked out the tournament page and found out someone beat me 
to Aioli's record by using 6 amulets of life saving. My 4 AoLS had no 
effect (I could have easily wished for better gear to pave the way). 
This game took me four days. Hmpf. Stupid genie...

